4.14.m:
On that second lunar day of generous release, the denizens of hell were gratified;
they were released from sins, all freed from bonds,
led about, made to dance, satisfied, staying wherever they pleased.

4.15.m:
May my householder’s life, which bestows dharma, artha, and kāma, not perish!
May the sacred fires not be lost; may the deities not be lost;
may the ancestors not be lost to me through division between husband and wife!
